Rāma halts on Tamasā bank and greets LakṣmaṆa --- Calls first forest night no cause for grief --- Pities empty wailing woods and mourning Ayōdhyā --- Trusts righteous Bharata to console parents --- Ceases grief recalling Bharata gentleness --- Lives on water only though wild food abounds --- LakṣmaṆa tells Rāma virtues to Sūta all night --- Orders swift dawn flight while followers sleep --- Fools seekers with northward feint then crosses Tamasā --- Citizens lose track and return grieving to Ayōdhyā
